    <h2 style="margin:52px 0 16px;color:#181818;font-size:34px;line-height:1.12;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-1.15px;">
        Choosing your one serum
    </h2>

    <p style="margin:0 0 22px;">
        The fastest way to waste a night routine is to use three actives at once. Choose by your main concern and keep the rest simple:
    </p>

    <ul style="margin:0 0 22px;padding-left:22px;">
        <li style="margin:0 0 10px;">
<strong>Oily, congested or breakout-prone skin:</strong> <a href="/products/acne-blemish-control-serum-30ml" style="color:#181818;text-decoration-color:#B87330;text-decoration-thickness:2px;text-underline-offset:4px;">Acne, Blemish Control Serum</a> contains salicylic acid and glycolic acid with niacinamide and Centella asiatica. Because it contains salicylic acid, check with a doctor first if you are pregnant or breastfeeding.</li>
        <li style="margin:0 0 10px;">
<strong>Dark spots, uneven tone or visible pores:</strong> <a href="/products/dark-spots-pore-control-serum-30ml" style="color:#181818;text-decoration-color:#B87330;text-decoration-thickness:2px;text-underline-offset:4px;">Dark Spots, Pore Control Serum</a> combines niacinamide, kojic acid, vitamin C, ceramides and Centella asiatica.</li>
        <li style="margin:0 0 10px;">
<strong>Dehydrated, dull or tight-feeling skin:</strong> <a href="/products/deep-hydration-glow-serum-30ml" style="color:#181818;text-decoration-color:#B87330;text-decoration-thickness:2px;text-underline-offset:4px;">Deep Hydration, Glow Serum</a> pairs vitamin C and niacinamide with five ceramides and cholesterol.</li>
    </ul>

    <p style="margin:0 0 22px;">
        Each serum is designed to be the active step in the routine, so you do not need to layer extra brightening or exfoliating products on top. Patch test before first use.
    </p>

    <h2 style="margin:52px 0 16px;color:#181818;font-size:34px;line-height:1.12;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-1.15px;">
        The moisturiser step
    </h2>

    <p style="margin:0 0 22px;">
        A moisturiser helps skin hold on to water. The barrier itself relies on fats between skin cells, which is why ceramides appear on so many labels.<a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/14728698/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank"><sup>3</sup></a>
    </p>

    <ul style="margin:0 0 22px;padding-left:22px;">
        <li style="margin:0 0 10px;">
<strong>Look for ceramides and hyaluronic acid.</strong> Dermatologists suggest both when scanning an ingredient list.<a href="https://www.aad.org/public/everyday-care/skin-care-basics/dry/pick-moisturizer" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank"><sup>4</sup></a>
</li>
        <li style="margin:0 0 10px;">
<strong>Skip fragrance and alcohol if your skin is dry or reactive.</strong> They can be irritating.<a href="https://www.aad.org/public/everyday-care/skin-care-basics/dry/pick-moisturizer" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank"><sup>4</sup></a>
</li>
        <li style="margin:0 0 10px;">
<strong>Choose a non-comedogenic label if you are oily or acne-prone.</strong> It means the formula is not meant to block pores.<a href="https://www.aad.org/public/everyday-care/skin-care-basics/dry/pick-moisturizer" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank"><sup>4</sup></a>
</li>
        <li style="margin:0 0 10px;">
<strong>Match the texture to your day.</strong> A light gel-cream suits oily skin or humid weather, and a richer cream suits dry skin or air-conditioned rooms.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 style="margin:52px 0 16px;color:#181818;font-size:34px;line-height:1.12;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-1.15px;">
        Starting a new serum
    </h2>

    <ul style="margin:0 0 22px;padding-left:22px;">
        <li style="margin:0 0 10px;">
<strong>Patch test first.</strong> Try a small amount on a small area before using it on your whole face.</li>
        <li style="margin:0 0 10px;">
<strong>Introduce it on its own.</strong> Use it alone for a week or two so you can tell how your skin responds.</li>
        <li style="margin:0 0 10px;">
<strong>Go slowly if your skin reacts easily.</strong> For Acne, Blemish Control Serum, the directions are to patch test first and start every other night if your skin is easily reactive.</li>
    </ul>

    <div style="margin:34px 0;padding:24px 26px;border-top:1px solid #B87330;border-bottom:1px solid #B87330;background:#FFFEF3;">
        <p style="margin:0 0 7px;color:#B87330;font-size:12px;line-height:1.2;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;">Keep in mind</p>
        <p style="margin:0;color:#181818;">
            Change one thing at a time. If you add a new serum and your skin starts to sting, pause it for a week, return to cleanser and moisturiser, and try again slowly.
        </p>
    </div>

    <h2 style="margin:52px 0 16px;color:#181818;font-size:34px;line-height:1.12;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-1.15px;">
        Mistakes that undo a night routine
    </h2>

    <ul style="margin:0 0 22px;padding-left:22px;">
        <li style="margin:0 0 10px;">
<strong>Stacking several actives.</strong> Irritation is the usual result, and it sets your routine back by weeks.</li>
        <li style="margin:0 0 10px;">
<strong>Using hot water.</strong> It leaves skin tight and more reactive to whatever you apply next.</li>
        <li style="margin:0 0 10px;">
<strong>Skipping moisturiser.</strong> Skin loses water more easily at night, so going without leaves it exposed.<a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/9424081/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank"><sup>2</sup></a>
</li>
        <li style="margin:0 0 10px;">
<strong>Rubbing and rushing.</strong> Press products in gently, and wait a minute between steps.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 style="margin:52px 0 16px;color:#181818;font-size:34px;line-height:1.12;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-1.15px;">
