    <h2 style="margin:56px 0 18px;color:#181818;font-size:34px;line-height:1.12;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-1.15px;">
        Frequently asked questions
    </h2>

    <div style="border-top:2px solid #181818;">
        <div style="padding:22px 0;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(24,24,24,.2);">
            <h3 style="margin:0 0 8px;color:#181818;font-size:21px;line-height:1.3;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-.25px;">What is the basic order of a night skincare routine?</h3>
            <p style="margin:0;">Cleanse, then apply a serum on damp skin, then moisturise. Lighter, water-based products go first and heavier creams go last.</p>
        </div>
        <div style="padding:22px 0;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(24,24,24,.2);">
            <h3 style="margin:0 0 8px;color:#181818;font-size:21px;line-height:1.3;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-.25px;">Should I apply my serum on damp or dry skin?</h3>
            <p style="margin:0;">For Acne, Blemish Control Serum, Dark Spots, Pore Control Serum and Deep Hydration, Glow Serum, the directions are 3 to 4 drops on damp skin. For other products, follow the directions on the pack.</p>
        </div>
        <div style="padding:22px 0;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(24,24,24,.2);">
            <h3 style="margin:0 0 8px;color:#181818;font-size:21px;line-height:1.3;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-.25px;">Do I need to double cleanse?</h3>
            <p style="margin:0;">Only if you wear heavy makeup or water-resistant sunscreen. On quiet days, a single wash with a gentle cleanser is enough.</p>
        </div>
        <div style="padding:22px 0;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(24,24,24,.2);">
            <h3 style="margin:0 0 8px;color:#181818;font-size:21px;line-height:1.3;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-.25px;">Can I use two serums at night?</h3>
            <p style="margin:0;">It is simpler and safer to use one targeted serum at a time. If you want to add a second product, introduce it on its own, a few days apart.</p>
        </div>
        <div style="padding:22px 0;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(24,24,24,.2);">
            <h3 style="margin:0 0 8px;color:#181818;font-size:21px;line-height:1.3;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-.25px;">Do I need sunscreen at night?</h3>
            <p style="margin:0;">No. Sunscreen belongs in your morning routine. Night is for cleansing, treating and moisturising.</p>
        </div>
        <div style="padding:22px 0;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(24,24,24,.2);">
            <h3 style="margin:0 0 8px;color:#181818;font-size:21px;line-height:1.3;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-.25px;">My skin stings after my night routine. What should I do?</h3>
            <p style="margin:0;">Pause the active serum and return to a gentle cleanser and a plain ceramide moisturiser until your skin is comfortable. If dryness becomes painful, cracked or very irritating, see a dermatologist.<a href="https://www.aad.org/public/everyday-care/skin-care-basics/dry/pick-moisturizer" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank"><sup>4</sup></a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

